From: Pharma360 QA Team
Subject: [PATCH 007/07] Fix nginx healthcheck to use curl instead of wget
Date: 2026-11-01

This patch fixes the nginx container healthcheck. The nginx:alpine image
doesn't have wget installed by default. We use curl which is more commonly
available or we can use a simpler check.

---
 docker/docker-compose.yml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docker/docker-compose.yml b/docker/docker-compose.yml
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/docker/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker/docker-compose.yml
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@ services:
       - ./frontend/dist:/usr/share/nginx/html:ro
     healthcheck:
-      test: ["CMD", "wget", "--no-verbose", "--tries=1", "--spider", "http://localhost/"]
+      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "curl -f http://localhost/ || exit 1"]
       interval: 30s
       timeout: 10s
       retries: 3
       start_period: 20s
---
To apply this patch:
  cd /workspace/github__DuDuEZN__Pharma-360
  patch -p1 < patches/007-fix-nginx-healthcheck-curl.patch

OR manually apply:
  1. Edit docker/docker-compose.yml
  2. Change line 172 from:
     test: ["CMD", "wget", "--no-verbose", "--tries=1", "--spider", "http://localhost/"]
     to:
     test: ["CMD-SHELL", "curl -f http://localhost/ || exit 1"]

Note: nginx:alpine doesn't have wget installed by default. Using curl is more
reliable. Alternatively, you could install wget in a custom nginx image.
